{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"id\":10980,\"title\":\"Have Gun, Will Travel\",\"tagline\":\"I don't think you got a very good look at this gun while you had it.\",\"overview\":\"Have Gun – Will Travel is an American Western television series that aired on CBS from 1957 through 1963. It was rated number three or number four in the Nielsen ratings every year of its first four seasons. It was one of the few television shows to spawn a successful radio version. The radio series debuted November 23, 1958.\\n\\nThe television show is presently shown on the Encore-Western channel.\\n\\nHave Gun – Will Travel was created by Sam Rolfe and Herb Meadow and produced by Frank Pierson, Don Ingalls, Robert Sparks, and Julian Claman. There were 225 episodes of the TV series, 24 written by Gene Roddenberry. Other contributors included Bruce Geller, Harry Julian Fink, Don Brinkley and Irving Wallace. Andrew McLaglen directed 101 episodes and 19 were directed by series star Richard Boone.\",\"posterPath\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/6aJRq7FGs2axLOdZNJ2G4IOQtMx.jpg\",\"backdropPath\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/original/7z1QYCB1cu06u3oJwIupRlZ8SrX.jpg\",\"youtubeBackdrop\":null,\"anilistBanner\":null,\"rating\":7.3,\"voteCount\":45,\"year\":1957,\"genres\":[\"Western\",\"Action & Adventure\",\"Drama\"],\"status\":\"Ended\",\"type\":\"tv\",\"totalSeasons\":6,\"totalEpisodes\":225,\"createdBy\":[\"Sam Rolfe\",\"Herb Meadow\"],\"networks\":[\"CBS\"],\"countries\":[{\"code\":\"US\",\"name\":\"United States of America\"}],\"lastAirDate\":\"1963-04-20\",\"cast\":[{\"id\":51875,\"name\":\"Andrew V. McLaglen\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/4Lxdxg5akHhsHoZToFe62L8RM9B.jpg\"},{\"id\":16420,\"name\":\"Richard Boone\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/dzvaoj0e25U69bWveXVBlhDkHPY.jpg\"},{\"id\":40402,\"name\":\"Buzz Kulik\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/qZuZuh3fyGnjjsOCW4323JaK1oy.jpg\"},{\"id\":1214133,\"name\":\"Lamont Johnson\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/oGqhGmjBntl4C0wVGDScr2u13Iw.jpg\"},{\"id\":46617,\"name\":\"Ida Lupino\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/nRRuTPNFNqpWpbXnIHjwPbLtCQp.jpg\"},{\"id\":30270,\"name\":\"Richard Whorf\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/mEPtqsnmOOvZmAouU5oOkNQkMSJ.jpg\"},{\"id\":7187,\"name\":\"Richard Donner\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/wjRecQiVLUAm6jwyT5craxhg3lD.jpg\"},{\"id\":16412,\"name\":\"William Conrad\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/3JgsIutm70SEfGqXTl0Gr3DQzAY.jpg\"},{\"id\":116986,\"name\":\"Jerry Hopper\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/4BXiHFsU6xRStKk26YyWfYGAWgl.jpg\"},{\"id\":47893,\"name\":\"Gary Nelson\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/mWOzNh1PfAhXW0exvkE2Dw0AJl3.jpg\"},{\"id\":2000,\"name\":\"Lewis Milestone\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/zcbvWlJTkFcVJ86Yjsvx82Mjgul.jpg\"},{\"id\":9108,\"name\":\"Don Taylor\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/6Gg2DR2oP3qUPTEomlJi7i4dne9.jpg\"},{\"id\":13861,\"name\":\"Frank Pierson\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/qB5v6C0gt4wa8tlxcuG90fF0Ye9.jpg\"},{\"id\":151445,\"name\":\"Jack Laird\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/sQfClv3voyUGM7cu3CYv1HA87aq.jpg\"},{\"id\":70262,\"name\":\"Elliot Silverstein\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/p7AyZ64osiltDxZLqvfNEFrjK1N.jpg\"},{\"id\":101767,\"name\":\"Robert Butler\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/zFkID35eoTJKZyEdfTmMe3kBBCJ.jpg\"},{\"id\":47370,\"name\":\"Paul Stanley\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":null},{\"id\":93943,\"name\":\"Gerald Mayer\",\"character\":\"Director\",\"photo\":null},{\"id\":16420,\"name\":\"Richard Boone\",\"character\":\"Paladin\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/dzvaoj0e25U69bWveXVBlhDkHPY.jpg\"}],\"trailers\":[{\"key\":\"TRNM8yqqqgU\",\"name\":\"Official Trailer\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"},{\"key\":\"Ei_pCruDAyg\",\"name\":\"Official Trailer\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"},{\"key\":\"JdYSlhCYKew\",\"name\":\"Official Trailer\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"}],\"similar\":[{\"id\":283304,\"title\":\"Little House on the Prairie\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/oWUGSadxC9vQPOCeHDDVfDezmQC.jpg\",\"rating\":6.7,\"year\":2026,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.2789115646258503,\"_genreOverlap\":2},{\"id\":62732,\"title\":\"Texas Rising\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/lnJLfFEpXgmTGUGzKqgHCsjYtMJ.jpg\",\"rating\":6.4,\"year\":2015,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.2758503401360544,\"_genreOverlap\":2}],\"seasonNumber\":2,\"seasonName\":\"Season 2\",\"seasonOverview\":\"The second season of Have Gun – Will Travel originally aired Saturdays at 9:30-10:00 pm on CBS from September 13, 1958 to June 20, 1959.\\n\\nThe Region 1 DVD was released on May 10, 2005.\",\"seasonPoster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/tuKnv9Al5OrbNSbZ7AREP1My4P9.jpg\",\"seasonAirDate\":\"1958-09-13\",\"episodes\":[{\"number\":1,\"name\":\"The Manhunter\",\"overview\":\"Paladin is forced to kill Jimmy Dawes, wanted for murder. When he takes him back to his home town, the townspeople, the sheriff and the boy's brothers give him a hostile welcome.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/cPuOuIA939uDI1kh0c43CXHJ7kg.jpg\",\"rating\":9,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-09-13\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"In an Evil Time\",\"overview\":\"Pappy French and his gang have robbed the bank in Mercede of $50,000. Pappy ran off with the cash and left his gang to shoot it out with the law. Paladin is hired to bring Pappy and the money back.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/iRWoyEL1iUoAyDCXBzyoSCqEVdm.jpg\",\"rating\":9,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-09-20\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"The Man Who Wouldn't Talk\",\"overview\":\"Chris Sorenson is shy around women and he asks Paladin to help him with his new neighbor, Senorita Maria de Castro, a lady rancher. Complicating the matter is cattle missing from the de Castro ranch.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/oPL6EJlcuyOAd1XW36CGRRbDz0U.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-09-27\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":4,\"name\":\"The Hanging of Roy Carter\",\"overview\":\"Roy Carter is scheduled to be hanged. Another man confesses to the murder just before the execution is to take place. Paladin is hired to try to convince the warden to delay the hanging until the Governor can be reached.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/NjHtfiD4CKalLHYTS12neUDOOc.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-10-04\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"Duel at Florence\",\"overview\":\"Paladin receives a letter with a bank draft for $82.17 from Ernie Teller asking for help with a matrimonial problem.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/31mzuiZbjLLQNJNZpcuKQ75vv9E.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-10-11\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"The Protege\",\"overview\":\"Paladin answers an ad in the paper by Kurt Sprague: \\\"\\\"Teach me to quick draw and shoot. Instruction desperately needed. Will pay one thousand dollars. Only experts need apply.\\\"\\\" Kurt needs to learn in order to go back home. Paladin does a very good job. Only one problem: Kurt enjoys showing off his new found skill a little too much.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/2pntUAdq1QS2rjU8YdiVmHlO5LC.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-10-18\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":7,\"name\":\"The Road to Wickenburg\",\"overview\":\"Paladin wakes up after being drugged, beaten and robbed in the town of Blue Bell by five men, one of whom is the town's sheriff. They took his money, gun, bullets, horse and saddle. All he has left is his two-shot derringer.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/6PCOaJoINpRhdzkgiwlhC6FhNCC.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-10-25\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":8,\"name\":\"A Sense of Justice\",\"overview\":\"The sheriff of a small town needs help to prevent the lynching of simple-minded Andy Dawes. The townspeople are sure he is a murderer. Paladin offers to help\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/6oqaXRGSwg3wwFPiy7CwnEqvYjV.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-11-01\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":9,\"name\":\"Young Gun\",\"overview\":\"An ex-gunfighter, Roy Calvert, blames the people of Benedict for his wife's death. The town is in the middle of a bad drought and Calvert and his son are blocking the only access to water in the area. Calvert has trained his son to be a gunfighter and Paladin has to face them both.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/6EcwAMA950i3jkGwX3cy2rPXx7k.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-11-08\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":10,\"name\":\"The Lady\",\"overview\":\"A British woman, Diana Coulter, hires Paladin to guide her to her brother's ranch in Shiprock, Arizona, where the Comanches are on the warpath.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/aKwAkHpccQTalFIxJnAbWBAgySk.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-11-15\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":11,\"name\":\"A Snare for Murder\",\"overview\":\"Two ornery old gold miners, who hate each other, have struck it rich. Problem is they talk too much, and now it appears someone is trying to kill them.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/spIhBPL7YsoIfE69HkvMjnDUkbv.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-11-22\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":12,\"name\":\"The Ballad of Oscar Wilde\",\"overview\":\"Paladin is hired to protect Oscar Wilde. Another 3 men apply for the job, but after Paladin upstages them they kidnap Wilde for ransom. Paladin takes care of them, his way.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/yckse24TyUHrf8KkbOp7c6iiv5n.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-12-06\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":13,\"name\":\"The Solid Gold Patrol\",\"overview\":\"Paladin goes to inform a calvary corporal that he has won $600,000 in a lottery. But they may not live to cash in the ticket, they are trapped by several dozen hostile Indians.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/hckVAcsYhn4R14p772OlekIn1I1.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-12-13\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":14,\"name\":\"Something to Live For\",\"overview\":\"On his way to help a man and his daughter over a land dispute, Paladin encounters a wealthy, drunk and helpless man whose guide left him behind to die.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/cstcFQaIAlJ4uzCf4uvkvaz9jqn.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-12-20\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":15,\"name\":\"The Moor's Revenge\",\"overview\":\"Shakespearean actors are going to perform in San Diego during their roundup. They are in for a rough reception. A lovesick gunfighter is among the audience. The show's promoter hires Paladin to keep the peace.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/pRAt3pI4HEDFBAnFZhpOdjKaYna.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1958-12-27\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":16,\"name\":\"The Wager\",\"overview\":\"Sid Morgan hires Paladin to protect him from someone who is trying to kill him. After killing the gunfighter who was following them, Paladin finds out the real reason Morgan hired him. He then hands out his own brand of justice.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/sRWIS2FCZdCrOvhucoXsWFpLTAy.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-01-03\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":17,\"name\":\"The Taffeta Mayor\",\"overview\":\"John Kellaway, who is running for mayor of Colton, Wyoming, hires Paladin to protect him from his opposition. When he is killed before Paladin can get there, Paladin persuades John's widow to run for mayor.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/xzV42rBfyJ29VwBnNqCpOiIMXic.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-01-10\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":18,\"name\":\"Lady on the Stagecoach\",\"overview\":\"Paladin is traveling on a stagecoach with four others, one of whom is Della White Cloud, the educated daughter of an Apache chief. The stage is also carrying a strongbox full of gold, which Ed Rance wants.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/65Jsb7cu6lLY2Tu9hcfDrf0w4QH.jpg\",\"rating\":9,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-01-17\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":19,\"name\":\"Treasure Trail\",\"overview\":\"Paladin wins part of a treasure map in a poker game and goes in search of the treasure with three other men.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ps7L2IYkV3NBHZV9aybfaIqDhWB.jpg\",\"rating\":9,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-01-24\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":20,\"name\":\"Juliet\",\"overview\":\"Juliet Harper is being hunted by the grandsons of Colonel Jeremiah Pike. Paladin meets her on the stage and now the Colonel is after both of them, and Paladin is without a gun.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/mvOWFDSTcJrraxPs3cpDEe093ei.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-01-31\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":21,\"name\":\"Hunt the Man Down\",\"overview\":\"Paladin finds himself reluctantly drawn into a deadly dispute between two brothers who are also old aquaintances.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/x8GeHhk2bCuxueUA0tZmrQiQVBr.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-02-07\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":22,\"name\":\"The Scorched Feather\",\"overview\":\"Robert Ceilbleu hires Paladin to protect his father from a Comanche war chief who has sworn to kill him. After arriving at the remote cabin of William Ceilbleu, he learns the reason for the Indian's hatred.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/bMjnGkqzt0yJotf7eWuvVoidl76.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-02-14\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":23,\"name\":\"The Return of the Lady\",\"overview\":\"Diana Coulter (The Lady, Episode 49) wires Paladin and asks him to come to her wedding to \\\"\\\"give the bride away\\\"\\\".\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/spZEGoz6X6J1d72stssrxNELWKF.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-02-21\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":24,\"name\":\"The Monster of Moon Ridge\",\"overview\":\"The townspeople of Moon Ridge, Colorado believe there are monsters in the mountains. Dan Bella's daughter is taken by something and he finds strange footprints outside his daughter's window. Paladin is hired to find out what is up on the ridge.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/6d9zAdr6YH3EOoyOKAzPsj43W6V.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-02-28\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":25,\"name\":\"The Long Hunt\",\"overview\":\"Thomas Orday, half Comanche, has killed two men and wounded Dundee, a former Indian fighter. He is now hiding in the mountains of New Mexico. Paladin is hired to help track him down.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/9G1aAdOPLSChDPSvdod14j5SLzS.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-03-07\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":26,\"name\":\"Death of a Gunfighter\",\"overview\":\"A ruthless gunfighter who has killed 9 men is wanted by the townspeople, who hire Paladin. The gunfighter's brother has been hanged and left out in the sreet to trap the gunfighter. On seeing this, Paladin quits the job. The gunfighter shows up and kills all the townspeople who were gunning for him. Then he and Paladin come to an agreement that if he hangs up his guns he can go back to his hometown to marry his sweetheart. But it turns out that she has fallen in love with someone else, and more trouble ensues.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/fGzoJWJMvHbW2mqKuZ4xmx6b3Ju.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-03-14\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":27,\"name\":\"Incident at Borrasca Bend\",\"overview\":\"Arriving in a weird tent town to return money to a prospector, Paladin finds himself charged with the man's murder and tried by a kangaroo court.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ucSJXtFawWvjZRRMnN5rgDprDyo.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-03-21\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":28,\"name\":\"Maggie O'Bannion\",\"overview\":\"After being bushwhacked and having 'everything' taken, Paladin walks to the nearest ranch and manages to get hired on as a handyman.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/yyoAX9DI6GjDLCsQyL7v1b1HcSW.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-04-04\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":29,\"name\":\"The Chase\",\"overview\":\"Paul Martin is a bank clerk accused of robbing the bank and killing a deputy. His wife hires Paladin to find her husband before the posse does.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/36UhzjnNziRuh7esTMe43UxCw4J.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-04-11\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":30,\"name\":\"Alaska\",\"overview\":\"Paladin play chess by mail with Boris, who is living in Alaska. Paladin receives what he assumes is Boris' next move but instead is a request for help. Boris is being forced out of territory he has hunted and trapped on for years. Paladin heads for Alaska to help.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/pvObnYpzUlk7UYkO0shzlYbPQPW.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-04-18\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":31,\"name\":\"The Man Who Lost\",\"overview\":\"Paladin goes after a man who murdered a man and attacked the man's wife. The victim's two brothers are also after him and don't intend to allow him to live long enough to stand trial.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/8sYSyDbJgeX93NwWl9etOSu0C0C.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-04-25\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":32,\"name\":\"The Return of Roy Carter\",\"overview\":\"Roy Carter returns to help Paladin search the snow-covered mountains for a missing chaplain and an escaped convict.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/x73cSI5bpCztbMoYW9wCIIghi1o.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-05-02\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":33,\"name\":\"The Sons of Aaron Murdock\",\"overview\":\"Paladin becomes a bounty hunter when a rancher hires him to bring in his son, who's become a sadistic, vicious killer.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/rRy553hq795SQ1YS98IJtV0X2Sh.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-05-09\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":34,\"name\":\"Comanche\",\"overview\":\"Paladin is hired to find a U.S. Army corporal, who is a deserter and the son of a general. Paladin must travel into Indian territory as he seeks the corporal. Along the way, Paladin encounters a soldier he knew from his own time in the Army. It turns out the corporal is part of the 7th Calvary, and is part of the command of George Custer.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/8rt05YGU0aTXEN1ZeWDzM03O2Wy.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-05-16\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":35,\"name\":\"Homecoming\",\"overview\":\"Wrongly convicted Ed Stacy, whom Paladin helped to put in prison, is being released after being pardoned. Will Stanhope, who runs the local freight office, hires Paladin to protect him from Stacy. Paladin soon wonders who is really in danger.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/3362Qhl5LX29bVvZKmSwtLb7Y7.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-05-23\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":36,\"name\":\"The Fifth Man\",\"overview\":\"Ben Talman, who has murdered 12 men, escaped from jail. He kills four men in Yucca Bend within one week. Paladin is hired to bring him in.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/hDyvd1BYR36b0EM6k65o2Z6r9gA.jpg\",\"rating\":8,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-05-30\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":37,\"name\":\"Heritage of Anger\",\"overview\":\"Paladin is hired to protect the Avery family from Manuel Garcia. Garicia is a Mexican bandit who seems to have taken a special interest in their son.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/9Mu6GWZZ0kvneUbHGPe7nAXRo0t.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-06-06\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":38,\"name\":\"The Haunted Trees\",\"overview\":\"Ben Howard is disinherited in his father's will. When his father dies, Mrs. Sarah Howard takes over running the family's  lumber company. She claims that Ben is sabotaging the work and scaring off the workers. Mrs. Howard hires Paladin to stop the problems and get rid of Ben.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/jl5k8JDykrYebqXE1p5IFAOQOUe.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-06-13\",\"runtime\":30},{\"number\":39,\"name\":\"Gold and Brimstone\",\"overview\":\"Paladin finds a sick old man and his son trying to protect their mine from claim jumpers. The old man is delirious and thinks that Paladin is the devil and has only offered to help in exchange for their souls.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/bNlKbFFws2KwGq7F368Iu3kVt4f.jpg\",\"rating\":7,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1959-06-20\",\"runtime\":30}],\"firstAirDate\":\"1957-09-14\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}